## Workflow Rules

### Planning
- Business strategy docs live under `.work.biz/plans/`.
- Wait for approval before creating substantial new strategy docs when the user asked for analysis only.

### Data loss & destructive operations

**Permission rule:** Explicit human approval is required for every action below. Approval applies **only to the current request (same message)** — it is never standing or permanent permission.

Unless the human operator explicitly requests it in the **same message**, agents MUST NOT:

| Action | Examples (non-exhaustive) |
|--------|---------------------------|
| **Git publish / rewrite** | `git commit`, `git push`, force-push, hard reset, `git clean -fd`, amend of published history, history rewrite (`rebase` that rewrites shared history), bypass hooks (`--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`) |
| **Database destroy** | `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, wipe, reset, or bulk-delete of any database, schema, table, volume, or equivalent datastore |
| **Filesystem delete** | Delete files or directories (`rm`, project-tree wipe, emptying generated artifact trees) |
| **Modify protected files** | Change items under **Protected Files** above without same-message permission |
| **Wipe project memory** | Bulk-delete or wipe `.work.biz/` trees (HANDOFF history, plans, pipeline, strategy) outside normal skill updates; replace an existing `.cursorrules` wholesale (merge only, or confirm overwrite when named in the same message) |
| **Commit secrets** | Commit API keys, credentials, or `.env` values into any tracked file |

Creating or editing files in declared task scope is allowed. Prefer reversible edits over delete or overwrite. When unsure, stop and ask.

### Git
- Commit/push only per **Data loss & destructive operations** above.
- Provide commit commands for the user when they will commit themselves (unless they explicitly asked you to run commit/push in the same message).

### No Attribution / No Signatures
- Do NOT add "Generated by", "Created by", dates, or agent signatures to files you create or modify.
- No `Co-authored-by:` trailers (mandatory). Enforced by hooks. Install: `bash scripts/install-git-hooks.sh`.

### Commit Message Format
- Subject: `BIZ-123: description` when ref known, else `type: description`.
- Valid types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`.

